		<section><p class="wide">An expired primary certificate can be a reason to use another approved relay, without trusting that expired certificate.
      <a href="/smtp-connection-failover.html#section-policy">Connection failover</a> provides separate opt-ins for authentication rejection and
      certificate verification failure. The selected destination still has to pass its own TLS checks, and mandatory message locks remain binding.</p></section>
